 ## Edge cases
@@ -61,6 +65,7 @@
 
 ## Failure modes
 
+- **agent-lint S030 / orphaned skill `.md` files**: six new `skills/design/scripts/*.md` files without SKILL.md citations or harness-sibling exclusions can fail `make lint` / `agent-lint --pedantic` while integration harnesses still pass. Earliest signal: S030 reports orphan skill files under `skills/design/scripts/`. Mitigation: add `Sibling: lib-plan-optional-trailers.md`, `Sibling: test-trailer-helpers.md`, and harness contract `test-trailer-awk.md` on the Plan helper contracts bullet; append stub-only `test-trailer-dedup.md`, `test-trailer-has-any.md`, and `test-trailer-validate.md` to the `agent-lint.toml` exclusion block (~1371+).
 - **Shard-coverage drift**: if a repo structural test requires every `test-*.sh` to map to a Makefile target/shard, an invoke-only `test-trailer-awk.sh` could trip it. Earliest signal: `make test-harness-shards-coverage` (or the equivalent check) fails. Mitigation: the existing thin adapters are already invoke-only and pass, so follow that precedent; if the check is stricter than expected, register `test-trailer-awk` as its own target + shard entry instead.
 - **Awk dialect / Bash 3.2 portability**: macOS `awk` (BWK) vs gawk differences, or a Bash 4-only construct, could make the harness pass locally but fail in CI (or vice versa). Earliest signal: harness output differs across `awk` implementations. Mitigation: use only POSIX awk features the unit-under-test already relies on, and run `make lint-bash32` plus the harness locally.
 - **BSD grep option swallowing on (3175) pins**: `grep -Fq '--snapshot-trailers'` without a `--` pattern terminator fails on BSD/macOS with `unrecognized option` before the structural test runs. Earliest signal: `make test-design-structure` aborts locally on macOS while passing in Linux CI (or vice versa if pins differ). Mitigation: use `grep -Fq -- '--snapshot-trailers'` / `grep -Fq -- '--dedup'` or `contains()` for each new literal hook pin.
